        rdfs:comment                   "Cover woven with a silk warp and a cotton weft, made in Europe, 18th century."@en , "Cover woven with a silk warp and a cotton weft with a series of broad yellow stripes alternating with a group of narrower ones in purple, white and light blue. The panel is backed with cotton and edged with gilt thread. The narrow stripes are woven in satin of 5 and the yellow stripes in 4/1 twill."@en ;
